From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: gate Uke charging on moisture and qualified faults

Add fixed moisture diagnostics, an enable-only detector path, qualified board
and battery guards, and an owned input-inhibit latch. The retained exact
OS3.0.304.0 module identifies XM input_suspend property 53; admit only this
fixed contract behind reviewed per-boot evidence. No raw XM API or pack limits.
Version-2 leases refuse older clients without external-temperature bounds.
Firmware readback does not establish electrical or wet-port acceptance.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig
@@ -211,6 +211,7 @@
 config BATTERY_QCOM_BATTMGR
 	tristate "Qualcomm PMIC GLINK battery manager support"
 	depends on QCOM_PMIC_GLINK
+	depends on IIO || !IIO
 	select AUXILIARY_BUS
 	help
 	  Say Y here to enable the Qualcomm PMIC GLINK power supply driver,
@@ -230,7 +231,9 @@
 	  operation without reviewed per-boot runtime admission. Exact active
 	  firmware, reply envelope, threshold semantics, measurement units and
 	  autonomous protection evidence must be reviewed before operations.
-	  No PD, current, voltage, factory or gauge control is enabled here.
+	  Version-2 leases also require fixed charger/connector IIO temperature
+	  ranges and moisture/input-suspend contracts. No raw vendor properties,
+	  PD, voltage, factory or gauge control is enabled here.
 
 config BATTERY_QCOM_BATTMGR_UKE_CURRENT
 	bool "Reviewed Uke constant-charge-current transport"
